From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mmdevapi: Drop stale Sony profile backend names

Default and Direct endpoints share a stable Windows MMDevice GUID, but the
device-name cache retained both backend names for that GUID.  GUID lookup then
returned whichever profile had first populated the cache.  After switching
from Direct to Default, new Death Stranding 2 effect streams consequently
tried to open the removed Direct PipeWire node; switching back happened to
work because that stale name became valid again.

When an opposite-profile endpoint replaces the active endpoint, remove every
backend mapping for the retained GUID and install only the newly published
name.  This keeps stream creation aligned with the active PipeWire profile
without changing the Windows endpoint identity.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c b/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c
--- a/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c
+++ b/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c
@@ -2017,16 +2017,20 @@
     for (i = 0; i < params->num; ++i)
     {
         const char *added_name = (const char *)params->endpoints + params->endpoints[i].device;
-        struct device *cached;
+        struct device *cached, *next;
 
         if (!is_dualsense_backend_name(added_name) ||
                 !dualsense_device_names_replace_profile(added_name, removed_name, params->flow))
             continue;
 
-        if ((cached = find_device_name_in_cache(added_name, params->flow)))
-            cached->guid = *guid;
-        else
-            add_device_to_cache(guid, added_name, params->flow);
+        LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY_SAFE(cached, next, &devices_cache, struct device, entry)
+        {
+            if (cached->flow != params->flow || !IsEqualGUID(&cached->guid, guid))
+                continue;
+            list_remove(&cached->entry);
+            free(cached);
+        }
+        add_device_to_cache(guid, added_name, params->flow);
     }
     LeaveCriticalSection(&devices_cache_cs);
 }
